{"name":"Foxfire Brown","hex":"#9f6949","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"foxfire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Bioluminescence created by some types of fungus, particularly those growing on rotting wood.","Wood exhibiting fungal bioluminescence; torchwood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foxfire"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Foxfire","blocks":[{"text":"Foxfire, also called fairy fire and chimpanzee fire, is the bioluminescence created by some species of fungi present in decaying wood. The bluish-green glow is attributed to a luciferase, an oxidative enzyme, which emits light as it reacts with a luciferin. The phenomenon has been known since ancient times, with its source determined in 1823."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/PanellusStipticusAug12_2009.jpg/330px-PanellusStipticusAug12_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foxfire"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Omphalotus_olearius_33857.jpg/500px-Omphalotus_olearius_33857.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna